# =============================================================================
# benchmarking 2 - what belongs in version control
# =============================================================================
#
# This tree is ~1.2 GB and almost all of it is regenerable tool output: 1,186
# antiSMASH regions, 83 staged BGC records, three BiG-SCAPE distance databases
# and a DiscERN run. None of that belongs in git. GitHub warns over 50 MB per
# file and rejects at 100 MB, and antiSMASH's per-genome JSON is ~11 MB each.
#
# So this file works by DENY-BY-DEFAULT: everything is ignored, and the code,
# documentation and small provenance tables are added back by name. A new data
# directory dropped into the tree is therefore ignored automatically, rather
# than silently committed because nobody updated a pattern.
#
# What ends up tracked is the handful of files needed to rerun the analyses,
# plus the tables that justify what was included and excluded. The data itself
# should go to a repository built for it (Zenodo, ENA/NCBI) and be cited from
# README.md by DOI or accession.
#
# To include the results after all, delete the "results" block near the end.
# To include the inputs too, delete the bulk-data lines - but read the size
# note above first, and expect to need Git LFS.

# --- deny everything at the top level, then re-admit ------------------------
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/PROJECT_SUMMARY.md
!/VERSIONS.txt

# --- step 1: raw genomes ----------------------------------------------------
!/raw/
/raw/*
!/raw/*.sh

# --- step 2: antiSMASH ------------------------------------------------------
!/antiSMASH/
/antiSMASH/*
!/antiSMASH/*.sh

# --- step 3: benchmark inputs and the run scripts ---------------------------
!/benchmark/
/benchmark/*
!/benchmark/*.py
!/benchmark/*.sh
!/benchmark/*.tsv

# the staged BGC records are regenerable from step 3; keep only the two
# tables that document why six genomes were held out of the analyses
!/benchmark/bigscape/
/benchmark/bigscape/*
!/benchmark/bigscape/excluded/
/benchmark/bigscape/excluded/*
!/benchmark/bigscape/excluded/*.md
!/benchmark/bigscape/excluded/*.tsv

# DiscERN: the patch is REQUIRED to rerun and is a few lines of diff, so it is
# tracked even though it sits inside a results directory
!/benchmark/discern/
/benchmark/discern/*
# The DiscERN patch is required to run the tool at all, so it is tracked even
# though it sits inside the analysis tree.
!/benchmark/discern/
/benchmark/discern/*
!/benchmark/discern/*.diff
!/benchmark/discern/*.tsv

# --- results: excluded for now ----------------------------------------------
# bigscape/results/ holds three SQLite distance databases and the BiG-SCAPE web
# UI. The .db files are the valuable part - they carry every pairwise distance,
# so a reader can re-cut at a different cutoff without rerunning - but they are
# large and regenerable. Deposit them rather than commit them.
/benchmark/bigscape/results/

# --- editor, OS and Python noise --------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*~
*.tmp
*.bak
